<pdd-reason>Per-plan dj notes are the gap that blocks everything else: one track must be able to carry different notes in two plans without losing the global note.</pdd-reason>
<pdd-interface>
{
  "type": "api",
  "api": {
    "endpoints": [
      {
        "method": "POST",
        "path": "/api/plans/<slug>/notes",
        "auth": "none",
        "requestSchema": "{track_id, note?, clear?: bool, author?: 'human'|'agent'|'llm', base_rev}",
        "responseSchema": "{rev, effective: {track_id, note, layer, diverged}}",
        "errors": [
          "400 unknown author value",
          "409 stale base_rev"
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
}
</pdd-interface>
<pdd-dependency>brain/plan_types_Python.prompt</pdd-dependency>
<pdd-dependency>brain/plan_revision_Python.prompt</pdd-dependency>
<pdd-dependency>brain/plan_journal_Python.prompt</pdd-dependency>
<pdd-dependency>brain/plan_notes_Python.prompt</pdd-dependency>
<pdd-dependency>brain/api_router_Python.prompt</pdd-dependency>

% Goal

Implement and maintain `brain/api/api_plan_notes.py` as the POST {track_id, note, author, base_rev} writes a TRACK-scoped plan override. POST {track_id, clear: true, base_rev} removes it, and the response shows the GLOBAL note that took over rather than an empty string, so the user can see what they fell back to. author is validated against plan_types.Author and recorded, so an LLM-written note stays distinguishable from a hand-written one. tracks.dj_notes is untouched by EVERY path through this route. One journal entry per accepted write with author propagated. Transition-scoped notes are not this route: they go through /api/plans/<slug>/transitions.

% Product contract

- Preserve the exact public interface declared in `<pdd-interface>`.
- Treat the reviewed architecture description in this prompt as normative behavior.
- Keep plan identity, immutable track identity, revision guards, and non-destructive storage semantics intact across GUI, CLI, and agent callers.
- Preserve compatible behavior outside this module's stated responsibility; do not redesign unrelated mixing or playback logic.
- Reject malformed, stale, ambiguous, or unsafe writes explicitly instead of silently losing plan data.
- Keep the implementation deterministic where the contract describes deterministic behavior.
- Target Python 3.13+ for Python modules and baseline browser JavaScript without a bundler for browser modules.
- Inspect the current implementation, its declared dependency modules, and the focused tests before changing code. This is a brownfield source prompt: working, tested behavior not contradicted here remains part of the contract.

% Architecture detail

POST {track_id, note, author, base_rev} writes a TRACK-scoped plan override. POST {track_id, clear: true, base_rev} removes it, and the response shows the GLOBAL note that took over rather than an empty string, so the user can see what they fell back to. author is validated against plan_types.Author and recorded, so an LLM-written note stays distinguishable from a hand-written one. tracks.dj_notes is untouched by EVERY path through this route. One journal entry per accepted write with author propagated. Transition-scoped notes are not this route: they go through /api/plans/<slug>/transitions.

% Output

- Primary output: `brain/api/api_plan_notes.py`.
- PDD context tags: backend, api, plan, notes.
- Keep changes scoped to the primary output and the smallest necessary caller/test adaptations.

% Verification

- Run the focused tests that cover `brain/api/api_plan_notes.py` and every declared interface.
- Run `UV_CACHE_DIR=/private/tmp/claw-dj-uv-cache uv run python -m unittest discover -s tests` before accepting a repository-wide sync.
- For Python modules, also run `UV_CACHE_DIR=/private/tmp/claw-dj-uv-cache uv run python -m py_compile brain/api/api_plan_notes.py`.
- Verify revision-conflict, missing-file, malformed-input, and legacy-compatibility paths relevant to this module.
- Do not require a model, GitHub, Mixxx playback, or network access for deterministic tests.

